      "round_summary": "Round 3/3 — fixed load_then_rotate_by_0 (assertion_error). Root cause: assertion compared io.dout against current io.din, but 2-cycle pipeline means io.dout reflects io.din from 2 cycles ago. Since io.din is an unconstrained free input that can change between cycles, formal tool finds counterexample by varying io.din at the check point. Fix: added `dinDelayed = RegNext(RegNext(io.din))` register to sample io.din with 2-cycle delay, and changed assertion to compare `io.dout === dinDelayed` instead of `io.dout === io.din`. Avoided `past()` due to curried-API compilation issue. Assertion label \"load_then_rotate_by_0\" preserved exactly. No homologous assertions exist.",
